| P2 | HLS audio discovery depended on TYPE being the first attribute. Non-playlist HTML and unsafe subresource URLs could also pass parsing. | Attribute order is independent, `#EXTM3U` is required, and unsupported/private-network addresses are rejected before fetching. Changing initialization maps is explicitly rejected; encrypted maps require an explicit IV. [playlist-parser.ts:105](<C:/Users/Nihil/Desktop/Github Repos/Draco/src/main/hls/playlist-parser.ts:105>), media parser fixtures. |

## Persistence, admission, browser, and renderer findings

| Priority | Trigger and previous behavior | Corrected behavior and evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| P1 | Startup continued after settings/task restore failure, allowing an empty manager to replace unreadable saved tasks. Concurrent retries could repeat restoration. | Dependent stages stop, task restore cannot be bypassed, and retries share one promise. [index.ts:509](<C:/Users/Nihil/Desktop/Github Repos/Draco/src/main/index.ts:509>), [tests/bootstrap-safety.test.ts](<C:/Users/Nihil/Desktop/Github Repos/Draco/tests/bootstrap-safety.test.ts>). |
